title: Revolt in Cabinet
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and cabinet_revolt >= 8
new-page: true

= Revolt in Cabinet

At the Cabinet meeting on public spending, the Treasury asks for another round of cuts. One by one, the wets refuse. It is the most open revolt against a Prime Minister by her own Cabinet in living memory, and by the evening it is in all the papers.

- @give_way: Give way on spending.
- @face_down: Face them down, and remember who spoke.

@give_way
on-arrival: spending += 1; budget -= 2; cabinet_revolt = 2; wet_dissent -= 6; dry_dissent += 8; thatcher_rating -= 2

The cuts are dropped. The wets have shown they can stop you.

@face_down
on-arrival: cabinet_revolt = 4; wet_dissent += 10; rebellion += 2; reshuffle_timer = 0; dry_dissent -= 4

The meeting ends without agreement and the cuts go ahead anyway, imposed department by department. A reshuffle is now only a matter of time.
